{"name":"Goldfish","hex":"#f2ad62","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Goldfish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small orange saltine-like cracker shaped in the form of a fish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Goldfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goldfish","blocks":[{"text":"The goldfish is a freshwater fish in the family Cyprinidae of the order Cypriniformes. It is commonly kept as a pet in indoor aquariums, and is one of the most popular aquarium fish. Goldfish released into the wild have become an invasive pest in parts of North America and Australia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Gold_fish1.jpg/330px-Gold_fish1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldfish","wikidata":"Q123141"},{"title":"Goldfish (cracker)","blocks":[{"text":"Goldfish is a brand of fish-shaped crackers with a small imprint of an eye and a smile manufactured by Pepperidge Farm, which is a division of Campbell's. The brand's current marketing and product packaging incorporate this feature of the product: \"The snack that smiles back! Goldfish!\", reinforced by Finn, the smiling goldfish mascot with sunglasses. The product is marketed as a \"baked snack cracker\" on the label with various flavors and varieties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Goldfish-Crackers.jpg/330px-Goldfish-Crackers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldfish_(cracker)","wikidata":"Q5580153"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Carassius_auratus_197778318.jpg/500px-Carassius_auratus_197778318.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Carassius_auratus_197778318.jpg/1280px-Carassius_auratus_197778318.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipe